# Language
  Identifier: sem-lang/standard/semantic
  Version: 0.10.0
  Dependencies: none

# Term
  Name: Value
  Description: A semantic value
  Meaning: Primitive/Value

# Term
  Name: Type
  Description: A semantic type
  Meaning: Primitive/Type

# Term
  Name: Predicate
  Description: A proposition-producing predicate
  Meaning: Primitive/Predicate

# Term
  Name: Relation
  Description: A relation among semantic values
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Role
  Description: A role held by an argument
  Meaning: Primitive/Role

# Term
  Name: Proposition
  Description: A proposition with truth conditions
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Reference
  Description: A reference to an identified value
  Meaning: Primitive/Reference

# Term
  Name: Variable
  Description: A bound or unresolved semantic variable
  Meaning: Primitive/Variable

# Term
  Name: Constraint
  Description: A constraint over semantic values
  Meaning: Primitive/Constraint

# Term
  Name: Composition
  Description: A composition of semantic expressions
  Meaning: Primitive/Composition

# Term
  Name: Quantification
  Description: Quantification over values
  Meaning: Primitive/Quantification

# Term
  Name: Polarity
  Description: Positive or negative polarity
  Meaning: Primitive/Polarity

# Term
  Name: Modality
  Description: Required, permitted, or possible modality
  Meaning: Primitive/Modality

# Term
  Name: Temporal
  Description: A temporal relation or value
  Meaning: Primitive/Temporal

# Term
  Name: Spatial
  Description: A spatial relation or value
  Meaning: Primitive/Spatial

# Term
  Name: Causality
  Description: A causal relation
  Meaning: Primitive/Causality

# Term
  Name: Entity
  Description: Something that can be referred to
  Meaning: Primitive/Value

# Term
  Name: State
  Description: A condition holding over an interval
  Meaning: Primitive/Value

# Term
  Name: Event
  Description: An occurrence situated in time
  Meaning: Primitive/Value

# Term
  Name: Action
  Description: An event attributable to an actor
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Agent
  Description: An entity capable of action
  Meaning: Primitive/Value

# Term
  Name: Change
  Description: A transition between states
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Intent
  Description: An intended state or action
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Plan
  Description: An ordered intention for action
  Meaning: Primitive/Composition

# Term
  Name: Commitment
  Description: An adopted obligation or intention
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Possession
  Description: A relation of possession
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Existence
  Description: Existence of a referent
  Meaning: Primitive/Predicate

# Term
  Name: Identity
  Description: Identity of a referent
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Part
  Description: A part of a whole
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Set
  Description: A collection of values
  Meaning: Primitive/Composition

# Term
  Name: Time
  Description: A temporal reference
  Meaning: Primitive/Temporal

# Term
  Name: Place
  Description: A spatial reference
  Meaning: Primitive/Spatial

# Term
  Name: Tomorrow
  Description: The day immediately following the context day
  Meaning: Primitive/Temporal

# Term
  Name: Near
  Description: A context-dependent spatial proximity relation
  Meaning: Primitive/Spatial

# Term
  Name: Create
  Description: Create a new value or state
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Update
  Description: Change an existing value or state
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Delete
  Description: Remove an existing value or state
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Infer
  Description: Derive a candidate from selected evidence
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Assertion
  Description: A communicated proposition
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Question
  Description: A request for information
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Request
  Description: A request for an action or result
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Proposal
  Description: A proposed action or state
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Report
  Description: A communicated observation or result
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Correction
  Description: A correction to an earlier proposition
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Confirmation
  Description: Confirmation of a proposition
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Rejection
  Description: Rejection of a proposition or request
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Delegation
  Description: Assignment of authority or work to another actor
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: BindingRequest
  Description: A request to establish a binding
  Meaning: Primitive/Proposition

# Term
  Name: Bind
  Description: Establish an explicit binding
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation

# Term
  Name: Cancel
  Description: Cancel an adopted action or state
  Meaning: Primitive/Relation
